+Values files are plain YAML files. A single values file may contain more than
+one YAML document (separated by `---`). When it does, the documents are merged
+in order, exactly as if each document had been passed as a separate `-f` file:
+later documents take precedence over earlier ones for overlapping keys.
+
+For example, `helm install -f many.yaml ./mychart` with a `many.yaml` like this:
+
+```yaml
+---
+replicas: 1
+---
+replicas: 2
+```
+
+is equivalent to `helm install -f a.yaml -f b.yaml ./mychart`, where `a.yaml`
+sets `replicas: 1` and `b.yaml` sets `replicas: 2`. The resulting value of
+`replicas` is `2`.
+
